t","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","number":16,"title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5790,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:48Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-09-08T23:47:36Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T10:40:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123321","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- As discussed [on RC](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/gdscript?msg=9iyRJYYRx2zPAaKx3) using coroutines as setter or getter can corrupt scenes. It's also generally bad practice because it can easily lead to bugs if you don't pay very close attention. In addition there is also the imminent risk of a coroutine getter returning a function state instead of the intended type, which might break code if the compiler does not account for it in some place.\r\n\r\n- As noted on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121322 mixing typed and untyped code for setter and getters (e.g. variable is typed but getter is not) could easily lead to runtime errors. In addition we also do not account for that all the time and don't generate the necessary type checks, which makes this very bug (and even crash) prone.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds warnings for those two anti patterns.\r\n \r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nIf we break compat in the future I think we should turn both of those into hard errors to safe ourself some complexity that the compiler needs to consider. But for now warnings should suffice.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123321/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123321/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}